Desugar models to check native propagation

Offer model desugaring independently of naive or seminaive matching so
the specialized propagation engine can be compared with ordinary rules.
Preservation materializes member facts at every nesting depth only when
the required morphism applications are defined. Existing membership
semantics and public APIs remain available in both modes.

Keep public input validation separate from derived tuple insertion so
preserved facts can arrive independently of their typing facts.

Desugared models use ordinary relation indices and fixed-point
evaluation, allowing cyclic morphism graphs without a topological
propagation phase. Include model mode in compiler cache keys and
exercise both evaluation strategies with partial applications,
nested relations, and cycles.
